---
import Base from '~/layouts/Base.astro';
---
<Base
  title="About — The Hey Bible Podcast"
  description="How the Hey Bible Podcast is made — public-domain text, AI voice, automated monthly releases."
>
  <section class="py-8 sm:py-12 max-w-[720px] mx-auto">
    <h1 class="text-3xl md:text-5xl font-extrabold mb-6">About</h1>

    <p class="text-lg opacity-90 mb-6">
      The Hey Bible Podcast was built to make the
      <a href="https://worldenglish.bible" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">World English Bible</a>
      — a complete, public-domain English translation of the Bible — more accessible by reading it aloud
      and publishing one book each month as a podcast. Free, ad-free, and works in any podcast app.
    </p>

    <h2 class="text-2xl font-extrabold mt-8 mb-3">A Working Dev’s Hero project</h2>
    <p class="opacity-90 mb-6">
      Hey Bible is a project from
      <a href="https://workingdevshero.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Working Dev’s Hero</a>,
      an AI-enabled software development company. The entire production pipeline — verse generation,
      chapter stitching, monthly book compilation, and release — was built end-to-end using
      <strong>OpenClaw</strong> running on
      <a href="https://venice.ai" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Venice.ai</a>.
    </p>

    <h2 class="text-2xl font-extrabold mt-8 mb-3">How it’s made</h2>
    <ul class="list-disc pl-6 opacity-90 space-y-2">
      <li><strong>Text:</strong> <a href="https://worldenglish.bible" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">World English Bible</a>, public domain — sourced from the WEB USFX XML in <a href="https://github.com/seven1m/open-bibles" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">seven1m/open-bibles</a>.</li>
      <li><strong>Voice:</strong> Generated with the “Bill” voice from ElevenLabs, called via the Venice AI API.</li>
      <li><strong>Hosting:</strong> Cloudflare — site (Workers Static Assets), audio files (R2), and DNS.</li>
      <li><strong>Source:</strong> <a href="https://github.com/Hey-Bible/hey-bible-podcast" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Open source on GitHub</a>.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2 class="text-2xl font-extrabold mt-8 mb-3">Schedule</h2>
    <p class="opacity-90">
      Verses are generated daily, chapters are stitched as soon as their last verse is recorded,
      books are compiled on the 25th of each month, and released as podcast episodes on the 1st.
      The full Bible is roughly 31,000 verses — about 75 hours of audio — which works out to several
      years of monthly book releases.
    </p>

    <p class="text-sm opacity-70 mt-12">
      Read the
      <a href="https://claudius.blog/blog/launching-hey-bible-podcast/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">launch announcement</a>
      for the longer story.
    </p>
  </section>
</Base>
